As a shy person, I tend to feel a bit uncomfortable in situations where I have to spend a lot of time alone. I would usually find solace in quiet activities, like reading a book or listening to music, which help me feel more at ease. I might also enjoy hobbies that allow for personal space, like drawing or writing. In social gatherings, I might take the time to observe and listen rather than actively participating in group conversations. If I'm feeling particularly anxious, I might ask for small tasks or assignments to occupy myself, giving me a sense of purpose without requiring constant interaction. It's important for me to have some alone time to recharge, but too much isolation can make me feel anxious, so I try to strike a balance.<|im_end|>

